      <!-- Section: Data Quality -->
      
        <div id="dataQuality" class="section metadataSection">
          <div class="section__header sh">
  <h2 class="sh__main" id="headerDataQuality">Data Quality</h2>
  
  
  
  
  

</div>
          <div class="section__content">
            
  

            
            
              
  <table class="name-value-table" aria-labelledby="headerDataQuality">
    
    
    
    <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Horizontal Positional Accuracy:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Compiled to meet 10 meters horizontal accuracy at 95% confidence level</p>

  </td>
</tr>
    
    
    
    
    
    
    
    
    
    
    <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Completeness Report:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>a) The geographic extent of these data include the conterminous United States, Hawaii, Guam, U.S. Virgin Islands and Puerto Rico.</p>
  <p>b) Presence, absence, and contiguity of a track is dependent on the distance, temporal, and navigational status filters applied in the track building algorithm. Parameters for these data were 1 nautical mile (1,852 meters), 30 minutes, and navigation status. Track features were further split by calendar day.</p>
  <p>c) It should be noted that navigation status is a product of operator input, so errors in the source data can exist. The navigation status as provided in the NMEA source data was not modified in these processed track data.</p>

  </td>
</tr>
    <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Conceptual Consistency:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>These data are logically consistent</p>

  </td>
</tr>
    
  </table>

            
          </div>
        </div><!-- .section Data Quality -->
      

      <!-- Section: Data Management -->
      

      <!-- Section: Lineage -->
      
        <div id="lineage" class="section metadataSection">
          <div class="section__header sh">
  <h2 class="sh__main" id="headerLineage">Lineage</h2>
  
  
  
  
  

</div>
          <div class="section__content">
            
            
  <table class="name-value-table" aria-labelledby="headerLineage">
    
  </table>

  
    <h3 class="record-block-section-header">Sources</h3>
    
      <div class="record-block">
        <div class="record-block-header cf">
          <h3 class="left force-break">U.S. Coast Guard Navigation Center</h3>
          <div class="x-small right">CC ID: <span>1502579</span></div>
        </div>
        <table class="name-value-table" aria-label="U.S. Coast Guard Navigation Center">
          
          
          
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Publish Date:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">2026-04-01</td>
</tr>
          
          
          
          
          
          
          
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Source Contribution:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Daily compressed log files containing original AIS messages in NMEA format for the United States</p>

  </td>
</tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    
  

  
    <h3 class="record-block-section-header">Process Steps</h3>
    
      <div class="record-block">
        <div class="record-block-header cf">
          <h3 class="left">Process Step <span>1</span></h3>
          <div class="x-small right">CC ID: <span>1502580</span></div>
        </div>
        <table class="name-value-table" aria-label="Process Step 1">
          <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Description:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>1. Filter the raw NMEA data to a one-minute sample rate and select a subset of fields using NMEA to SQL Server processing tools</p>
  <p>2. Load filtered records to an SQL Server 2026 database using NMEA to SQL Server processing tools</p>
  <p>3. Conduct quality and completeness check using logging results from the filter and loading process</p>
  <p>4. Update the imo, call_sign, vessel_name, vessel_length, width, and vessel_type fields from the AIS Vessel Identification Database (AVID) where original AIS values are missing</p>
  <p>5. Add a new vessel_type_name code to each record fragment that originated from the AIS Vessel Identification Database</p>
  <p>6. Develop track line features directly from the SQL Server database using NMEA to SQL Server processing tools for each month of broadcast records using a filter of 1 nautical mile (1,852 meters), 30 minutes, and navigation status</p>
  <p>7. Split track features by calendar day</p>
  <p>8. Add vessel_type_name field and populate based on the vessel type code to vessel group mapping described in the Vessel Type Codes list</p>
  <p>9. Add duration_minutes field and calculate the time in minutes between the start and end time for each track feature</p>
  <p>10. Perform visual quality and consistency checks and remove vessel tracks that are clearly invalid (on land) or beyond the ocean basin</p>
  <p>11. Repair Geometry to correct features with null geometry, self intersections, and other errors</p>

  </td>
</tr>
